    summary_60s: 'Direct Speech Direct speech, also called quoted speech, is when we write or say the exact words spoken by a person. These words are enclosed in quotation marks (" ") and remain unchanged. It is often used in conversations, storytelling, and interviews. Examples of Direct Speech: ',
