    summary_60s: 'Antonyms are words with opposite meanings. They help us understand language by setting one idea against another. When you hear the word “smooth,” the contrasting idea “rough” may immediately come to mind. In this pair, “rough” is the antonym of “smooth.” Other examples include: v',
