    summary_60s: 'Stress is the stronger or louder syllable in a word. We pronounce one syllable more clearly and loudly than the others. Examples: TA ble → stress on the 1st syllable a BOUT → stress on the 2nd syllable COM pu-ter → stress on the 1st syllable We often show stress like this: TA ble',
