    summary_60s: 'Emphatic stress is the placing of emphasis on a particular word of a sentence for clarity purpose, comparison, highlighting of ideas or connection of ideas. In simple terms, emphatic stress is like putting a spotlight on a word in a sentence. It\'s done by speaking the word with m',
